From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:05:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: mtu3: reconnect after a suspend taken with a suspended
 bus

With a suspended bus allowed to suspend the system, the gadget can go
to sleep still marked connected. The system suspend powers the device
IP and port down, which drops the link and the D+ pullup, and resume
powers them on again without either: on the Gemini the gadget stayed
"not attached" after a replug until a soft disconnect and connect from
userspace.

Doing that disconnect at suspend does not work: taking the pullup down
on a suspended bus keeps the IP from sleeping ("ip sleep failed") and
the system suspend aborts. So leave the suspend as it is and repeat the
userspace cure at resume: report the disconnect a VBUS drop would have,
drop the connection's runtime PM reference, and cycle the pullup so the
host can enumerate the device afresh.
---
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h      |  1 +
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
index 320a5e37e..597bb4b49 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
@@ -368,6 +368,7 @@ struct mtu3 {
 	unsigned gen2cp:1;
 	unsigned connected:1;
 	unsigned bus_suspended:1;
+	unsigned reconnect_on_resume:1;
 	unsigned async_callbacks:1;
 	unsigned separate_fifo:1;
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
index ecae7a057..2b8f38617 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
@@ -1045,6 +1045,12 @@ int ssusb_gadget_suspend(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg)
 	if (mtu->connected && !mtu->bus_suspended)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
+	/*
+	 * Leave the suspended link as it is, or the IP will not sleep: the
+	 * reconnection waits for resume.
+	 */
+	mtu->reconnect_on_resume = mtu->connected;
+
 	mtu3_dev_suspend(mtu);
 	synchronize_irq(mtu->irq);
 
@@ -1060,5 +1066,34 @@ int ssusb_gadget_resume(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg)
 
 	mtu3_dev_resume(mtu);
 
+	/*
+	 * The power-down dropped the link and the D+ pullup, so the host has
+	 * to enumerate the device afresh: report the disconnect that a VBUS
+	 * drop would have, then cycle the pullup, which resume alone does not
+	 * restore.
+	 */
+	if (mtu->reconnect_on_resume) {
+		unsigned long flags;
+
+		mtu->reconnect_on_resume = 0;
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&mtu->lock, flags);
+		if (mtu->softconnect)
+			mtu3_dev_on_off(mtu, 0);
+		mtu->connected = 0;
+		mtu->bus_suspended = 0;
+		mtu3_gadget_disconnect(mtu);
+		mtu->g.speed = USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mtu->lock, flags);
+		/* The reference the connection took in mtu3_link_isr(). */
+		pm_runtime_put(mtu->dev);
+
+		if (mtu->is_active && mtu->softconnect) {
+			usleep_range(10000, 20000);
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&mtu->lock, flags);
+			mtu3_dev_on_off(mtu, 1);
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mtu->lock, flags);
+		}
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
-- 
